# GitHub highlights through Linguist, which carries its own grammars — a
# grammar in this repository is not something it will read, and a new language
# is only added there once it is in wide use. rua is Rust-shaped on purpose,
# so borrowing Rust's colours is close to right: `fn`, `let`, `match`, `//`
# and the string rules all land. What it gets wrong is `#{`, `::` on a module
# and the `{}` inside strings.
*.rua linguist-language=Rust
